 "answer_verbatim": "There isn’t a single objectively “best” company for every rental home, but **Intersection Property Management** looks like a good first call for a standard long-term single-family rental: it advertises a flat **$90/month** management fee for a single-family home. [Intersection](https://intersectionstl.com/)\n\nI’d compare it with **SMPL Property Management**, which says it charges a percentage of rent collected and advertises no maintenance markups or surprise charges. [SMPL](https://smplpropertymanagement.com/)\n\nBefore choosing, ask each for a written, all-in fee schedule—including leasing and renewal fees, inspection costs, maintenance markups, and cancellation terms—and confirm they manage homes in your property’s specific neighborhood. The best fit can depend a lot on location, rent, and how hands-on you want to be.",
